---
import CodeBlock from "../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro";
import ModelSection from "../../components/models/ModelSection.astro";
import ModelLayout from "../../layouts/ModelLayout.astro";
import { sectionLookup } from "../../lib/models";

const sections = [
  {
    id: "how-it-works",
    title: "How it works",
  },
  {
    id: "model-at-a-glance",
    title: "Model at a glance",
  },
  {
    id: "example-input-and-output",
    title: "Example input and output",
  },
  {
    id: "examples-for-underwriting-and-risk-engineering-teams",
    title: "Examples for underwriting and risk-engineering teams",
  },
  {
    id: "quickstart",
    title: "Quickstart",
  },
  {
    id: "evaluation-base-models-and-data",
    title: "Evaluation, base models and data",
  },
  {
    id: "limitations",
    title: "Limitations",
  },
  {
    id: "license-and-citation",
    title: "License and citation",
  },
];
const section = sectionLookup(sections);
---

<ModelLayout slug="nouli-underwrite-evidence" sections={sections}>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Organize historical construction-incident evidence into four review themes. Three local models
      combine their answers; separate rules route the supplied case for information, referral or
      human review.
    </p>
    <p class="release-scope">
      Research preview for commercial underwriters and risk engineers. Requires a supplied
      supporting excerpt and separate current facts. People make final underwriting decisions.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
  <ModelSection {...section("how-it-works")}>
    <p>
      <img
        src="/models/nouli-underwrite-evidence/how-it-works.svg"
        alt="A supplied historical narrative and a human-selected excerpt go to three local models. Their combined answer gives a review theme. Separate rules check current supplied facts and route the case for information, referral or human review."
      />
    </p>
    <p>
      The ensemble classifies the historical evidence. Separate rules check the supplied current
      facts, conflicts and delegated authority. Nouli connects these steps and records the workflow.
      Missing or conflicting required information bypasses the classifier; a person retains the
      final decision.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("model-at-a-glance")}>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Property</th>
          <th>Value</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Input</td>
          <td>An English historical incident narrative and a human-selected supporting excerpt</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Output</td>
          <td>One of four review themes, all probabilities and component outputs</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Themes</td>
          <td>
            Equipment/control integrity; Management/training; Work practice; Worksite condition
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Workflow</td>
          <td>Information request, referral or progression to human review under example rules</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Models</td>
          <td>RoBERTa-large, TS-Ettin-150M and Ettin encoder 1B</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Size</td>
          <td>Approximately 1.54B parameters in total; 3.07 GB of stored weights</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Runtime</td>
          <td>Local CPU or CUDA; CPU rechecked for this release</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Licenses</td>
          <td>
            Apache-2.0 and MIT;{" "}
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/LICENSES.md">
              component notices
            </a>{" "}
            apply
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("example-input-and-output")}>
    <p>
      <strong>Historical evidence excerpt:</strong> “truck brakes failed”
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Context:</strong> A historical road-construction incident involving a water truck at a
      paving project. The complete original narrative accompanies the excerpt in the{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/input.json">
        input packet
      </a>
      . For the workflow demonstration, separate constructed documents supply a verified
      current-control status and a requested limit of USD 500,000, within the example authority
      limit.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Recorded output</strong> (abridged):
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Recorded output"
      code={`{
  "learned_output": {
    "label": "Equipment/control integrity"
  },
  "routing": {
    "recommendation": "PROCEED_TO_UNDERWRITER_REVIEW",
    "review_team": "engineering_controls_review",
    "human_final_decision": true
  }
}
`}
    />
    <p>
      The ensemble identifies an equipment issue in the historical evidence. The example rules then
      send the packet to engineering-controls review. Progression means a human review step, not
      insurance approval.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/output.json">
        Complete recorded output
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("examples-for-underwriting-and-risk-engineering-teams")}>
    <p>
      These examples cover all four themes. Each was run on CPU through the native Nouli workflow
      with its full historical narrative. The excerpts come from the source training partition and
      illustrate behavior; they are not an independent accuracy test. Suggested follow-up documents
      are supplied workflow guidance, not model-generated findings about current controls.
    </p>
    <details class="model-example-group" open>
      <summary>
        Equipment/control integrity<span>Recorded CPU example</span>
      </summary>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Supplied historical excerpt</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>truck brakes failed</p>
        </blockquote>
        <CodeBlock
          label="Recorded output"
          code={`{
  "learned_output": {
    "label": "Equipment/control integrity"
  },
  "routing": {
    "review_team": "engineering_controls_review"
  }
}
`}
        />
        <p>
          <strong>Current evidence to review:</strong> A dated equipment inspection and remediation
          verification.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-01-input.json">
            Complete input
          </a>{" "}
          ·{" "}
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-01-output.json">
            Recorded output
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="model-example-group">
      <summary>
        Management/training<span>Recorded CPU example</span>
      </summary>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Supplied historical excerpt</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>employer did not ensure adequate ground and truss bracing were installed</p>
        </blockquote>
        <CodeBlock
          label="Recorded output"
          code={`{
  "learned_output": {
    "label": "Management/training"
  },
  "routing": {
    "review_team": "management_training_review"
  }
}
`}
        />
        <p>
          <strong>Current evidence to review:</strong> A current hazard-management and supervision
          plan.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-02-input.json">
            Complete input
          </a>{" "}
          ·{" "}
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-02-output.json">
            Recorded output
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="model-example-group">
      <summary>
        Work practice<span>Recorded CPU example</span>
      </summary>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Supplied historical excerpt</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>He inadvertently stepped off the roof</p>
        </blockquote>
        <CodeBlock
          label="Recorded output"
          code={`{
  "learned_output": {
    "label": "Work practice"
  },
  "routing": {
    "review_team": "work_practice_review"
  }
}
`}
        />
        <p>
          <strong>Current evidence to review:</strong> The current safe-work procedure and
          verification of its use.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-03-input.json">
            Complete input
          </a>{" "}
          ·{" "}
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-03-output.json">
            Recorded output
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="model-example-group">
      <summary>
        Worksite condition<span>Recorded CPU example</span>
      </summary>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Supplied historical excerpt</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>unprotected floor edge</p>
        </blockquote>
        <CodeBlock
          label="Recorded output"
          code={`{
  "learned_output": {
    "label": "Worksite condition"
  },
  "routing": {
    "review_team": "worksite_conditions_review"
  }
}
`}
        />
        <p>
          <strong>Current evidence to review:</strong> An updated site assessment and evidence of
          protective controls.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-04-input.json">
            Complete input
          </a>{" "}
          ·{" "}
          <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/themes/theme-04-output.json">
            Recorded output
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <p>
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/theme-examples.json">
        Complete inputs, probabilities and recorded outputs
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <h3>Handling incomplete information and referrals</h3>
    <p>The supplied cases also demonstrate the checks around the classifier:</p>
    <table class="underwrite-workflow-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Situation</th>
          <th>Recorded workflow behavior</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Required facts are present</td>
          <td>Classify the historical evidence and apply the review rule.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Current-control information is missing</td>
          <td>Request information; skip classification.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Supplied current-control information conflicts</td>
          <td>Refer to an underwriter; skip classification.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Requested limit exceeds delegated authority</td>
          <td>Refer to senior-underwriter review.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Historical supporting evidence is absent</td>
          <td>Request information; skip classification.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The declared authority limit changes</td>
          <td>Apply the new rule to the same historical model input.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      These are constructed rule demonstrations, not observed carrier decisions. The USD limits, 0.8
      probability threshold and team mappings are illustrative.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/examples/workflow-examples.json">
        Recorded workflow cases
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("quickstart")}>
    <p>
      Use Python 3.12 and the{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/huggingface_hub/guides/cli">HF CLI</a>. Download the
      complete repository:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal"
      code={`hf download nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence --revision v1.0.0 \\
  --local-dir ./nouli-underwrite-evidence
cd nouli-underwrite-evidence
python3.12 verify_release.py
python3.12 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
.venv/bin/python inference/predict.py --checkpoint . --device cpu \\
  --text-file examples/model-input.txt --output outputs/prediction.json
`}
    />
    <p>
      The provided helper runs the complete ensemble. The root is a custom package; a raw
      Transformers <code>pipeline</code> or <code>AutoModel</code> call will not run all three
      models. All weights and tokenizers are included. No hosted API key or separate base download
      is required.
    </p>
    <p>
      To run the evidence checks and routing through{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/nouli-ai/nouli/releases/tag/v0.5.1">Nouli CLI 0.5.1</a>:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal"
      code={`.venv/bin/python inference/nouli_demo.py --checkpoint . --device cpu \\
  --nouli /absolute/path/to/nouli \\
  --case examples/input.json --rules examples/portable/rules-v1.json \\
  --output outputs/workflow.json
`}
    />
    <p>
      See{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/GETTING_STARTED.md">
        setup and integration
      </a>{" "}
      for preparing your own evidence packet, hardware requirements, offline use and the local
      provider endpoint.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("evaluation-base-models-and-data")}>
    <p>
      The supplied frozen evaluation records <strong>86.79% macro-F1</strong> and{" "}
      <strong>91.06% accuracy</strong> on 123 examples from 106 source reports. Inputs include
      human-selected supporting excerpts. These results measure historical evidence-theme
      classification, not performance on raw submissions or underwriting outcomes.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/evaluation.json">
        Evaluation scope and metrics
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      Based on <a href="https://huggingface.co/FacebookAI/roberta-large">RoBERTa-large</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/typestrict/TS-Ettin-150M">TS-Ettin-150M</a> and{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-1b">Ettin encoder 1B</a>, using{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/lab-flair/constructcie">ConstructCIE</a>, a
      human-annotated dataset of historical construction accident narratives.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/provenance.json">
        Pinned revisions and provenance
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("limitations")}>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Requires a supplied, source-supported excerpt. Automatic evidence extraction and end-to-end
        processing of raw insurance submissions were not evaluated.
      </li>
      <li>
        Historical incidents do not establish present controls. Current assertions must cite
        separate supplied documents; the workflow does not independently verify those assertions.
      </li>
      <li>
        The benchmark is small and imbalanced, with few management/training examples in the held-out
        set. Performance across carriers, trades and document types remains unmeasured.
      </li>
      <li>
        Each component has a finite input budget. Keep the relevant excerpt first and follow the
        supplied serialization; long context can be truncated.
      </li>
      <li>
        Probabilities and the example review threshold are not guarantees of correctness. The rules
        require validation for the intended workflow.
      </li>
      <li>
        Coverage, liability, regulatory compliance, pricing, acceptance and binding decisions are
        outside scope. No insurer or source-data publisher endorsement is implied.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("license-and-citation")}>
    <p>
      Nouli's runtime additions and the TS-Ettin component use Apache-2.0; upstream MIT notices
      apply to RoBERTa and Ettin. ConstructCIE annotations are Apache-2.0. Preserve the{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/LICENSES.md">
        component licenses
      </a>
      ,{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/LICENSE">
        LICENSE
      </a>{" "}
      and{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/NOTICE">
        NOTICE
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://nouli.ai">Nouli AI</a>. Nouli Underwrite Evidence. Cite the published version
      and commit. ConstructCIE is attributed in{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-underwrite-evidence/resolve/88e1585d1876a754adf36d32a253b693bc49439b/LICENSES.md">
        LICENSES.md
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
</ModelLayout>
